<title>USA: Witco Q1 net shr $0.35 vs $0.46.</title>
<headline>Witco Q1 net shr $0.35 vs $0.46.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>WITCO CORP AND SUBSIDIARY COS</p>
<p>						 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						     March 31,</p>
<p>				    1997 (A)(B)(C)    1996 (A)(C)</p>
<p> Net Sales			  $568,490,000   $589,425,000</p>
<p> Gross Profit			136,325,000    141,080,000</p>
<p>   Restructuring charge	    3,538,000		 --</p>
<p> Net Income			   19,939,000     25,921,000</p>
<p> Net Income Per Common Share:	   0.35	     0.46</p>
<p>Average Number of</p>
<p>   Common Shares		    57,064,000     56,895,000</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>(A) Depreciation expense for the three months ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	  and 1996, respectively, was $22,825,000 and</p>
<p>$25,317,000.  Amortization</p>
<p>	  expense for the respective periods was $6,066,000, and</p>
<p>$7,411,000.</p>
<p>(B) The restructuring charge of $3,538,000 ($2,158,000 after-tax or $.04</p>
<p>	  per common share) for the three month period ended</p>
<p>March 31,1997</p>
<p>	  primarily relates to expenditures for equipment at</p>
<p>sites previously</p>
<p>	  identified for closure, which otherwise would have</p>
<p>been capitalized.</p>
<p>(C) The three month periods ended March 31, 1997 and 1996 include gains of</p>
<p>	  $950,000 ($580,000 after-tax or $.01 per common share)</p>
<p>and $2,936,000</p>
<p>	  ($1,791,000 after-tax or $.03 per common share) as a</p>
<p>result of</p>
<p>	  settlements with certain of the company's insurers,</p>
<p>net of related</p>
<p>	  legal and other costs.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
